another's:
He sings to the dewy morn,
No thought of another's ear;
But the song he sings is a chant for kings

anon:
Consoled the race of mastodons to know
Before they went to fossil, that anon
Their place should quicken with the elephant;

Through the roar of wind and waters
Ever and anon she cried;
But throughout the night of terror

anoint:
Must melt down golden pieces in the nard
Wherewith to anoint her broomstick ere she rides;
And poets evermore are scant of gold,

anodyne:
But long before the drug could tell,
He took his anodyne;
With scornful grace, he bowed farewell

anothah:
Dey 's anothah hummah
Sings anothah song instid;
An' his th'oat 's a-swellin'

Evahthing I see erbout me 's jes' lak sunshine in de spring;
An' it seems lak I do' want to do anothah blessid thing
But jes' run an' tell de neighbours, an' to shout an' pray an' sing.

But seem lak she los' huh sperrit, all huh darin'ness was daid.
Did n't cut anothah capah nary time de blessid night;
But de othah one, hit looked lak could n't git enough delight.

In de noons o' summah
Dey 's anothah hummah
Sings anothah song instid;

anodynes:
And then, excuse from pain;
And then, those little anodynes
That deaden suffering;
